{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"31d2b8ebf1f69ba4ac66cb0b4080ed41f0ed5f232b522f159a0a11c2a0b67620","digest":{"component_or_area":"review-bot git fetch","key_entities":["src/rebar/_snapshot/repo_snapshot.py","src/rebar/_snapshot/git_fetch.py","src/rebar/review_bot/voter.py","_fetch_origin","http.lowSpeedLimit","http.lowSpeedTime","_GIT_TIMEOUT","_interprocess_lock","_fetch_lock_for","resolve_ref"],"problem_keywords":["git fetch stall","timeout abort","throughput detection","low-speed abort","review bot","subprocess hang"],"propositions":["Review bot's git fetch hangs intermittently for up to 300 seconds due to missing throughput-keyed abort on byte-starved connections; root cause is absent http.lowSpeedLimit and http.lowSpeedTime git config options.","Stalled fetch (connection established, zero bytes transferred) should abort in ~10 seconds via throughput-floor detection rather than wall-clock timeout.","Legitimately slow but progressing fetches must not be aborted; the threshold must be keyed on throughput, not elapsed time, demonstrated by dribbling-remote test.","Low-speed abort failures should be retried in-process a bounded number of times while non-low-speed failures (auth, bad ref) should not be retried, enabling transient stalls to self-heal within a single review."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787524365597117001,"uuid":"8533204b-dc68-49d4-86cc-a455a0c13027"}